note store/clone.om: the clone panel of the store-reading build, composed after dl/dl.om in place of
note dl/dlclone.om (run.sh units with FORGE_STORE). It never shows a rad clone line. The Git over
note HTTPS line is shown only when the build was given a clone base (FORGE_CLONE_BASE, FSCB 1 in
note .build/store.om): <base>projects/<name>/repo.git, the store's own layout. The archive links are
note dl/dlclone.om's. The agent line of dl/dlclone.om (forge-contribute, which opens a Radicle
note patch) is left out: proposals move to Interplane's own records (interplane-native DESIGN.md
note step 3).
text tscl1 "<details class=\"clone pj-get\"><summary class=\"pj-btn\">Get this repository</summary><dl>"
text tscl2 "<dt>Git over HTTPS</dt><dd><code>git clone "
text tscl3 "</code></dd>"
text tscl4 "<dt>Source archive of "
text tscl5 "</dt><dd><a href=\""
text tscl6 ".zip\">Download ZIP</a> &middot; <a href=\""
text tscl7 ".tar.gz\">tar.gz</a></dd></dl></details>\n"
fn dlclone to void
dldefbr
fput tscl1
if eq FSCB 1
i = get fridx 0
if lt i get fan 0
fput tscl2
fesc tfcbase
fesc tfsprj
fputrn i
fesc tfsrg
fput tscl3
end
end
fput tscl4
dlescref
fput tscl5
dlrepol
fput tdarhh
dlescref
fput tscl6
dlrepol
fput tdarhh
dlescref
fput tscl7
end
